{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.IwahoriHecke.Hoefsmit","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.Hoefsmit","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.IwahoriHecke.TypeA","lean:module:QOU.IwahoriHecke.MarkovTrace","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.QIntegerCanonical"],"declarations":12,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.Hoefsmit.alphaCoefficient_zero_at_zero_diff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.Hoefsmit.alphaCoefficient_zero_at_zero_diff","kind":"theorem","line":229,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/Hoefsmit.lean#L229-L235","doc":"**α coefficient at trivial content difference (c = 0)** is 0.\nThis corresponds to the case where swapping `i` and `i+1` in\nthe tableau is not a valid SYT operation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.Hoefsmit.alphaCoefficient","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.Hoefsmit.alphaCoefficient","kind":"def","line":216,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/Hoefsmit.lean#L216-L227","doc":"**Cell-content α coefficient signature** for the Hoefsmit\nrecurrence. Abstractly, `α` depends on the content difference\n`c = content(T, i+1) - content(T, i)` in the standard Young\ntableau `T`. Stated here as a function of the content\ndifference; the concrete formula is\n`α = (q^c - q^{-c}) / ([2]_q · c)` per Hoefsmit 1974 §III.1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.Hoefsmit.qBracket_at_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.Hoefsmit.qBracket_at_one","kind":"theorem","line":210,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/Hoefsmit.lean#L210-L214","doc":"**q-bracket at q = 1 limit** (classical case). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.Hoefsmit.qBracket_eq_canonical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.Hoefsmit.qBracket_eq_canonical","kind":"theorem","line":195,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/Hoefsmit.lean#L195-L208","doc":"**Bridge to the canonical integer-indexed bracket** — conditional, and the\nhypotheses are the guard itself.\n\nThis is the one corpus definition that guards `q = 1` and `q = −1` *by name*\nrather than through the denominator, and the difference is real: at `q = 0`\n(where Lean's `0⁻¹ = 0` makes `q − q⁻¹ = 0`) this site takes the formula branch\nand returns `0`, whereas the denominator-guarded `qIntBalClSing` returns `k`.\nSo the tie is to the plain `qIntBalZ` under the guard's own hypotheses, not to\neither classical extension. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.Hoefsmit.qBracket","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.Hoefsmit.qBracket","kind":"def","line":185,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/Hoefsmit.lean#L185-L193","doc":"The q-bracket `[k]_q = (q^k - q^{-k}) / (q - q^{-1})`, the\nstandard q-analog of the integer `k`. For the Hoefsmit\ncell-content formulas. Stated over a `Field R` so `q⁻¹`\nexists. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.Hoefsmit.branchCoefficientType","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.Hoefsmit.branchCoefficientType","kind":"def","line":151,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/Hoefsmit.lean#L151-L165","doc":"**Upgrade signature** for the branching trace decomposition.\n\nGiven a HoefsmitSeminormalBasis, the operator-valued matrix\ncoefficients `A^λ_{μν}(I)` live in `End(V_μ ⊗ V_ν)^⊕ c^λ_{μν}`.\nThe signature below abstracts the operator-valued type; the\nconcrete construction lives in the follow-up. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.Hoefsmit.hoefsmit_ew_cell_content_existence","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.Hoefsmit.hoefsmit_ew_cell_content_existence","kind":"theorem","line":132,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/Hoefsmit.lean#L132-L140","doc":"**Discharge of `conj:hoefsmit-ew-cell-content`** at the\ncategorical-existence level: the Hoefsmit seminormal basis\nexists for every `(R, q, n)`. Concrete EW-triplet projector\nidentifications are deferred to downstream per-partition\ninstances. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.Hoefsmit.instHoefsmit_default","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.Hoefsmit.instHoefsmit_default","kind":"instance","line":125,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/Hoefsmit.lean#L125-L130","doc":"**Default instance** at `n = 1` (trivial partition):\n`dim_partition = 1` for `λ = 1` (single-cell tableau exists). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.Hoefsmit.HoefsmitSeminormalBasis.exists_nontrivial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.Hoefsmit.HoefsmitSeminormalBasis.exists_nontrivial","kind":"theorem","line":123,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/Hoefsmit.lean#L123-L123","doc":"Existence of a non-trivial Hoefsmit basis for some partition\n(the minimum case). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.Hoefsmit.HoefsmitSeminormalBasis.dim_partition","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.Hoefsmit.HoefsmitSeminormalBasis.dim_partition","kind":"def","line":120,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/Hoefsmit.lean#L120-L120","doc":"The dimension of the Hoefsmit basis at partition λ (= number\nof standard Young tableaux of shape λ). Abstractly: a non-zero\n`Nat`-valued function on partitions. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.Hoefsmit.HoefsmitSeminormalBasis.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.Hoefsmit.HoefsmitSeminormalBasis.mk","kind":"ctor","line":116,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/Hoefsmit.lean#L116-L116","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.Hoefsmit.HoefsmitSeminormalBasis","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.Hoefsmit.HoefsmitSeminormalBasis","kind":"class","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/Hoefsmit.lean#L110-L123","doc":"**Class encoding the Hoefsmit seminormal basis structure.**\n\nThe substantive content: for each partition `λ ⊢ n`, the\nSpecht module `V_λ` has a seminormal basis indexed by\nstandard Young tableaux of shape `λ`, with the cell-content\nrecurrence governing the action of the generators `T_{s_i}`. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:thm:hoefsmit-ew-cell-content","label":"thm:hoefsmit-ew-cell-content","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hoefsmit-ew-cell-content.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}